{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Vanishing Ideal.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Vanishing Ideal.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"vanishing ideal vanishing ideal","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Vanishing Ideal.md","fileName":"Vanishing Ideal.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Vanishing Ideal","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-13 19:50\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Affine Geometry and Schemes]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Affine Geometry and Schemes","Ideal","Affine Variety","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Vanishing Ideal.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Vanishing Ideal.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"vanishing ideal vanishing ideal","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Vanishing Ideal.md","fileName":"Vanishing Ideal.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Vanishing Ideal","heading":"Vanishing Ideal","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The vanishing ideal I(V) of a subset V of affine space consists of all polynomials that evaluate to zero at every point of V. It is an [[Ideal]] because sums and polynomial multiples of vanishing functions also vanish.\n\nAn [[Affine Variety]] is recovered as the common zero set of an ideal. The relationship reverses inclusion: adding equations shrinks the point set, while adding points reduces the collection of polynomials that vanish everywhere.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Affine Geometry and Schemes","Ideal","Affine Variety","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Vanishing Ideal.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Vanishing Ideal.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"vanishing ideal vanishing ideal","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Vanishing Ideal.md","fileName":"Vanishing Ideal.md","